{"name":"Bridge Troll Grey","hex":"#817f6e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bridge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A construction or natural feature that spans a divide.\n A construction spanning a waterway, ravine, or valley from a height, allowing for the passage of vehicles, pedestrians, trains, etc.","A construction spanning a waterway, ravine, or valley from a height, allowing for the passage of vehicles, pedestrians, trains, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be or make a bridge over something.","To span as if with a bridge."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bridge"},{"term":"troll","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a giant supernatural being, especially a grotesque humanoid creature living in caves or hills or under bridges. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A type of diminutive supernatural being; a dwarf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Senses relating to a rolling motion.\n\nTo move (something, especially a round object) by, or as if by, rolling; to bowl, to roll, to trundle. \n\n Often followed by in: to cause (something) to flow or roll in like a stream.\n\nTo roll; also, to turn round and round; to rotate, to spin, to whirl. \n\nTo move or walk at a leisurely pace; to ramble, to saunter, to stroll. \n\n Chiefly of a man: synonym of cruise (“to stroll about to find a (male) sexual partner”). \n Followed by in: to flow or roll in like a stream.","To move (something, especially a round object) by, or as if by, rolling; to bowl, to roll, to trundle. \n\n Often followed by in: to cause (something) to flow or roll in like a stream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/troll"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Troll","blocks":[{"text":"A troll is a being in Nordic folklore, including Norse mythology. In Old Norse sources, beings described as trolls dwell in isolated areas of rocks, mountains, or caves, live together in small family units, and are rarely helpful to human beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/John_Bauer_1915.jpg/330px-John_Bauer_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troll","wikidata":"Q12581"},{"title":"Bridge","blocks":[{"text":"A bridge is a structure designed to span an obstacle, such as a river or railway, allowing vehicles, pedestrians, and other loads to pass across. Most bridges consist of a flat deck, supported by beams, arches, or cables. These structures rest on a foundation that is carefully designed to transfer the weight of the bridge to the subsoil without settling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Bridge_Alcantara.JPG/330px-Bridge_Alcantara.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bridge","wikidata":"Q12280"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Theodor_Kittelsen_-_Forest_Troll_-_NG.K%26H.B.03222_-_National_Museum_of_Art%2C_Architecture_and_Design.jpg/500px-Theodor_Kittelsen_-_Forest_Troll_-_NG.K%26H.B.03222_-_National_Museum_of_Ar